# Copy to .env and fill in only what you need.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local storage - what a plain laptop run uses, and all that tests need.
# Leave this whole section alone unless you're deploying somewhere that
# wipes local disk on restart (e.g. Render's free tier - see below).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
LGD_DB_PATH=records.db
LGD_ARCHIVE_DIR=archive

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Landlords and logins live in accounts.json, not here.
#   python -m app.accounts init
#   python -m app.accounts set-password kevin
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Render + Supabase deployment (free tier, no credit card).
#
# Leave every line below blank to run entirely on local files, exactly as
# above - this is what tests do. Set them only when deploying somewhere
# (e.g. Render's free web service) whose local disk does not survive a
# restart:
#
#   DATABASE_URL   - a Supabase Postgres connection string. Replaces
#                    LGD_DB_PATH for records, and also makes accounts.json
#                    switch to Postgres `landlords`/`users` tables (see
#                    `python -m app.accounts` for managing them there).
#   LGD_ARCHIVE_DIR - set to "supabase:<bucket-name>" to keep files
#                    in a Supabase Storage bucket instead of local disk.
#                    Create the bucket yourself in the Supabase dashboard
#                    first; nothing here creates it.
#   SUPABASE_URL, SUPABASE_KEY - only needed when LGD_ARCHIVE_DIR above
#                    points at a supabase: bucket. Project Settings > API.
#                    Use the service_role key, not the anon key: the
#                    landlord dashboard is the only thing writing to the
#                    bucket, and it already enforces its own auth.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DATABASE_URL=
# SUPABASE_URL=
# SUPABASE_KEY=
